# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# uv
uv.lock.bak

# CatBoost training-run artifacts (written to cwd by default during .fit())
catboost_info/

# Data / models / state (all reproducible from ingestion; never committed)
data/**
!data/.gitkeep
models/**
!models/.gitkeep
predictions/**
!predictions/.gitkeep
reports/**
!reports/.gitkeep
# Narrow, deliberate exceptions (M17 draft-engine forensic audit): unlike everything else
# under reports/, these two are NOT reproducible from `alpha-squad ingest` -- they are raw
# diagnostic evidence from a specific ~42-minute forensic run, and three tracked documents
# (docs/DRAFT_ENGINE_FORENSIC_AUDIT.md, docs/DRAFT_CONTROLLED_EXPERIMENTS.md,
# docs/DRAFT_ENGINE_REDESIGN_RECOMMENDATION.md) cite them as their evidence base. Ignoring
# them would leave those documents pointing at dangling evidence after a fresh clone.
!reports/draft_decision_trace.json
!reports/draft_forensics_experiment_results.json
# D55 adds two more: the P-tier ablation that chose the shipped formula, and the
# post-implementation re-trace proving the mechanism (not just the roster counts) changed.
!reports/draft_forensics_ptier_results.json
!reports/draft_decision_trace_d55.json
# D58/D60 (1-QB format retarget): the M-tier ablation that chose marginal starter value over
# VORP as the score's value base, and the pick-level counterfactual attribution both
# docs/FORMAT_MIGRATION_DIAGNOSTIC.md (S7-8) and docs/DECISIONS.md D60 cite as their evidence.
# Same reasoning as the M17/D55 exceptions above: not reproducible without redoing the full
# ingest/train/market pipeline, so kept alongside the documents that cite them.
!reports/draft_forensics_mtier_results.json
!reports/pick_attribution.json
# W1.1/D110 (weekly program): the FantasyPros API boards are NOT reproducible from
# `alpha-squad ingest` and, unlike everything else here, cannot be re-fetched at will -- the
# configured key is a public tier (`limit: 10` rows per board) with a request quota that
# exhausted during the harvest. Two tracked documents
# (docs/weekly/W11_FANTASYPROS_FLEX_AUDIT.md, docs/weekly/W2_ECR_BENCHMARK_RESULTS.md) cite
# them as the evidence that a real weekly FLEX board exists and that the mirror reconstruction
# reproduces it. Same reasoning as the M17/D55/D58 exceptions above. Each board carries a
# `content_sha256` so a later re-harvest can be diffed rather than silently replacing this
# vintage. Contains only ranking + player identity: no schedule or roster field is retained,
# because those are not historical in this payload (D110 §3).
# Git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded DIRECTORY, so the directories are
# un-ignored first, then the files inside them.
!reports/weekly/
!reports/weekly/fp_api_cache/
!reports/weekly/fp_api_cache/**
# The W2 benchmark output the results document quotes throughout. Reproducible in principle,
# but only after a full ingest + feature build, and it is the artifact a future phase diffs
# against to check the benchmark has not drifted.
!reports/weekly/w2_results.json
# W3/D111: the Alpha-vs-ECR-vs-baseline benchmark output. Reproducible only after a full
# 2015-2025 ingest, feature build and model training run (~hours); the results document quotes
# it throughout and a later phase diffs against it to check the baseline has not drifted.
!reports/weekly/w3_results.json
# W4/D112: the FLEX forensic audit -- 14 systems x 79 weeks of cells, the oracle/counterfactual
# boards, the exact pairwise decomposition, composition and per-season robustness. Same
# reasoning as w3_results.json: it needs the same multi-hour ingest/train run to regenerate,
# docs/weekly/W4_FLEX_FORENSICS_RESULTS.md quotes it throughout, and W4 itself demonstrates why
# the artifact matters -- it reproduces w3_results.json value-for-value (max abs diff 0), which
# is only checkable because the earlier file is tracked.
!reports/weekly/w4_results.json
# W5/D113: the top-of-board forensic audit -- per-cell metrics for four systems x four
# positions, the calibrated copula-null distribution, the exact player-level regret
# decomposition (~16k player-weeks) and the cohort attribution. Same reasoning as w3/w4: it
# needs the same multi-hour ingest/train run to regenerate, docs/weekly/W5_TOPBOARD_FORENSICS.md
# quotes it throughout, and W5's own reproduction gate diffs it against w3_results.json and
# w4_results.json -- which is only checkable because those files are tracked.
!reports/weekly/w5_results.json
# W5/D113 (E1): the exploratory miss-predictability diagnostic. Small, but the results document
# quotes its AUCs and permutation baselines, and a later phase re-reads them to check whether the
# "misses are unpredictable" finding still holds against a changed model.
!reports/weekly/w5_e1.json
# W6/D114: the upper-outcome experiment. Five trained arms x four positions x 79 weeks of
# per-cell metrics, the per-arm copula-null cliff re-test, the movement diagnostics, and the
# board-agreement measurements that explain the null (rank correlation 0.99+ between the treated
# and control boards). Reproducible only after the same multi-hour ingest and feature build;
# docs/weekly/W6_UPPER_OUTCOME_RESULTS.md quotes both files throughout, and the W6 gates diff
# them against fresh runs -- which is only checkable because they are tracked.
!reports/weekly/w6_results.json
!reports/weekly/w6_agreement.json
# W7/D115: the opportunity-forecastability audit. 150 forecast cells x 79 weeks, the ranking
# ladder (Alpha + pre-Friday opportunity vs production), rank bands, LOSO / per-season and Half-PPR.
# docs/weekly/W7_OPPORTUNITY_RESULTS.md quotes it throughout and the W7 G10 gate diffs it against a
# fresh run -- which is only checkable because it is tracked.
!reports/weekly/w7_results.json
# W8/D116: the ECR-advantage decomposition (per-week G/G_F/G_S/G_C, pair tests, buckets,
# counterfactual boards, player level, LOSO/per-season, Half-PPR) and the exploratory Class-A
# falsification check. docs/weekly/W8_ECR_ADVANTAGE_RESULTS.md quotes both throughout; the W8
# gates diff w8_results.json against a fresh run -- only checkable because it is tracked.
!reports/weekly/w8_results.json
!reports/weekly/w8_null_check.json
# W9/D117: durable / weekly / efficiency decomposition of ECR's usage edge (per-week boards,
# residualized anticipation, tiers, weekly classes, periods, Half-PPR, FLEX, counterfactual, player
# level). docs/weekly/W9_MECHANISMS_RESULTS.md quotes it and the W9 gates diff it against a re-run.
!reports/weekly/w9_results.json
# W10/D118: Alpha + prior-season role/production vs current Alpha (per-week cells for every arm,
# periods, LOSO/per-season, decomposition, cliff, misses, movement, calibration, redundancy) and
# the post-hoc B-vs-null check. docs/weekly/W10_HISTORICAL_RESULTS.md quotes both; the W10 gates
# diff w10_results.json against a re-run.
!reports/weekly/w10_results.json
!reports/weekly/w10_posthoc.json
state/**
!state/.gitkeep
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Frontend
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Claude Code agent worktrees (isolation:"worktree" sub-agents), never project content
.claude/
